1  CPWATCH                              A VM/370 Online Monitor
0                    A VM/370 Online Monitor
+                    _______________________

-       CPWATCH is  an online  performance monitor  for VM/370.
   It displays enough about the current activity of CP to allow
   an intuitive grasp of system  load, gross conflicts, and the
   currently active users.
0     It displays its output on DIALled local 3270 Model 2's.

-  History
+  _______
0          This monitor  was written originally by  Gary George
   at COMINCO Ltd, Trail, B.C.,  Canada, and contributed to the
   Waterloo library.
        It is now being maintained at the Workers' Compensation
   Board of Alberta.
        Marten Kemp of Data  Management Design contributed code
   for the  display of allocated  paging/spooling space  on the
   System panel.

-  Recent Changes
+  ______________
-       4.1 - paging device information.
+       4.1
0       4.2 - automatic detection of target operating sys-
+       4.2
             tem level.  Add  missing interrupt recogniser
             (for  dialled  devices) to  prevent  lockout.
             Use selector channel protocol.
0|      4.3 -  add VMCF interface.  Change  PFkey settings
+       4.3
 |           to conform to CMS conventions.  Correct logic
 |           errors.

