-  CPWATCH 4.3                - 2 -            02 December 1984

1  CPWATCH                                          DESCRIPTION
0                          DESCRIPTION
+                          ___________

-  CURRENT STATE
+  _____________
0     Operational,  stabilized.  Running  on  a 3083-E16  under
   VM/SP 3.1 HPO 3.2.

-  Access
+  ______
0|    CPWATCH can  be accessed  using the  CP DIAL  command, or
 | from a CMS machine using VMCF.
 |
 |    To access using DIAL:
 |         CP DIAL userid
 | Where "userid"  is the name  of the virtual  machine running
 | the monitor, usually 'CPWATCH'.
 |
 |    Using VMCF, the CMS MODULE "CPWCMS" is used:
 |        CPWCMS Ýscreen-name¨ Ý( Ý SERVER userid ¨¨
 | Note that module "CPWCMS" has the userid "CPWATCH" wired in,
 | but it can be overridden from  the command line. (It can, of
 | course, be changed permanently by recompiling CPWCMS).
 |
 |    The first screen displayed shows a menu of available com-
 | mands.

